hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24222","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdillah al-Yazani, from Hudhayfah al-Azdi, from Junadah al-Azdi, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday, with seven men of al-Azd, I being their eighth, while he was eating lunch. So he said: Come to lunch. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we are fasting. He said: Did you fast yesterday? He said: We said: No. He said: Will you fast tomorrow? He said: We said: No. He said: So break your fast. He said: So we ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When he came out and sat on the pulpit, he called for a vessel of water and drank while on the pulpit, with the people looking, showing them that he does not fast on Friday."
